\label{rem:scope}
Three levels:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item \textbf{One-parameter, restricted:}
  Factorization on $\im(\delta_L)$ (integrands linear in $z$).
\item \textbf{Two-parameter, $\nu$-regular:}
  Factorization on $\im(\widetilde{\delta}_L)$
  (integrands in $L^p(\nu)$, including all Leibniz defects).
\item \textbf{Full representation:}
  Against $\widetilde{N}(ds,dz)$ for all $L^1$-martingales, but
  without norm control.
\end{enumerate}
Theorem~B operates at the duality-pairing level and requires none of
these representation properties.

