\label{thm:martinelli}
Let $\mu$ be a Gibbs measure with finite-range interactions on
$G^{|E(\Z^d)|}$ for a compact group~$G$.  Suppose there exists a
block size~$L_0$ such that:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item \textbf{Uniform block gap:} For all boundary conditions~$\sigma$:
  \begin{equation}\label{eq:ubg}
    \gamma_0 := \inf_\sigma \gap(\Lambda_{L_0}, \sigma) > 0.
  \end{equation}
\item \textbf{Single-site gap:} The conditional measure on each site,
  given all other sites, has spectral gap $\ge c_0 > 0$ for all
  boundary conditions.
\end{enumerate}
Then the infinite-volume Glauber dynamics has a positive spectral gap:
\begin{equation}
\gap(\mathcal{L}_{\Z^d}) \ge c(\gamma_0, c_0, L_0, d) > 0.
\end{equation}

\label{thm:ubg}
For the $\mathrm{SU}(2)$ Yang--Mills Hamiltonian at $j_{\max} = 1$
on the open $2^3$ block with arbitrary boundary conditions
$\sigma \in \{0, \tfrac{1}{2}, 1\}^{12}$:
\begin{equation}
\gamma_0(g^2) = \min_\sigma \gap(\Lambda_2, \sigma, g^2) > 0
\qquad \text{for all } g^2 \in \{0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0, 8.0\}.
\end{equation}

