\label{prop:ric-AG}
The Ricci curvature of $\cA/\cG$ with the $L^2$ metric receives
two contributions:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:ric-decomp}
  \Ric_{\cA/\cG} = \underbrace{\Ric_G}_{\ge \rho_G > 0}
  + \underbrace{\Ric_{\mathrm{orbit}}}_{\ge 0},
\end{equation}
where:
\begin{enumerate}[nosep]
\item $\Ric_G$ is the fiber Ricci curvature inherited from the
  compact group $G$, with $\Ric_G \ge \rho_G > 0$.
\item $\Ric_{\mathrm{orbit}} \ge 0$ is the O'Neill curvature
  correction from the Riemannian submersion
  $\cA \to \cA/\cG$, which is always nonnegative.
\end{enumerate}

In particular, $\Ric_{\cA/\cG} \ge \rho_G > 0$.

\label{thm:sufficient}
