< \frac{2}{E}\Bigl(\sum_j p_j^2\Bigr)\Pi(J).
\end{equation}
In the special case $\Pi(J)=\sum_k T(k)=0$ (which holds
when the nonlinear term conserves $\Hdot{1/2}$ energy),
this simplifies to:
\begin{equation}
