\label{conj:defect}
Let $Y$ be an admissible process in the $(D,\delta,\Pi)$ framework, with enough regularity to make \eqref{eq:defect_general} meaningful. Then for a class of nonlinear transforms $\varphi$ containing at least $\varphi(x)=e^x$ and, on positive domains, $\varphi(x)=\log x$, the defect $\mathfrak D_t^{\varphi}(Y)$ is determined by the intrinsic bracket:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:defect_bracket}
