\label{rem:leibniz}
The operator--covariant derivative $D_X = \delta_X^*$ is \emph{not} a derivation in general. For products $FG$ of smooth functionals, the failure of Leibniz is encoded in a cocycle or correction term that depends on the quadratic variation or jump structure of $X$. Explicitly:
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item For continuous martingales, $D_X(FG) = F \cdot D_X G + G \cdot D_X F + \Gamma_X(F,G)$, where $\Gamma_X$ is related to the carr\'e du champ operator.
\item For jump processes, additional terms arise from the compensated sum over jumps.
\end{enumerate}

