- c_p \frac{a!}{(a+1-p)!}\int_0^u X_s^{a+1-p}(T-s)^{b}\, ds,
\end{equation}
where the last term is present only when $a+1 \geq p$, and the second term only when $b \geq 1$.

\label{prop:telescope}
For every $p \geq 2$ and $n \geq 1$,
