\label{thm:gaussian_axioms}
In the Gaussian setting, axioms \textnormal{(A1)--(A5)}
hold with $K(t) = 0$.  Axiom \textnormal{(A6)} is
vacuous (the defect $C_t \equiv 0$).

\label{thm:levy_axioms}
In the L\'evy setting, axioms \textnormal{(A1)--(A6)}
hold with $K(t)$ bounded by the jump measure content
on $[0,t]$.

