\label{thmB}
Let $p_t$ be the marginal density of $X_t$ under~\eqref{eq:VL-forward-intro}. Under standard regularity (Section~\ref{sec:score}), the score is
\begin{equation}\label{eq:score-VL}
  \nabla_x \log p_t(x) \;=\; \underbrace{-\frac{x - c(t)\, m(x,t)}{v_W(t)}}_{\text{Gaussian part (Tweedie)}} \;+\; \underbrace{\frac{1}{p_t(x)}\,\partial_x J_t(x)}_{\text{jump part}},
\end{equation}
where $m(x,t) := \E[X_0 \mid X_t = x]$, $v_W(t) := \sigma^2 \|\varphi_t\|^2_{\HW}$ is the intrinsic continuous bracket, and $J_t(x) = \int p_{t,J}(x - y)\,p_{t,W}(y)\,dy$ is the convolution of the jump law with the Gaussian law conditional on $X_0$, integrated over $X_0$.

Equivalently, via Bismut--Skorokhod integration by parts on the combined energy space,
\begin{equation}\label{eq:score-bismut}
