\begin{enumerate}[(A1),nosep]
\item \textit{Adjointness}: $\delta_X = D_X^*$ (the divergence is the Hilbert-space adjoint of the derivation);
\item \textit{Chain rule}: $D(\varphi(Y)) = \varphi'(Y)\,DY$ for smooth $\varphi$ and $Y \in \dom(D)$;
\item \textit{Orthogonal projection}: $\Pi = \Pi^*$ on $L^2(\Omega; \calH)$;
\item \textit{Energy regularity}: $\Gamma^X(t) := \|\Pi DX_t\|_{\calH}^2 \in \BV[0,T]$.
\end{enumerate}
Then the second-order correction in the operator It\^o formula is uniquely determined by the energy function: for $\varphi \in C^3_b(\R)$,
