\partial_t p = H t^{2H-1} \Delta p.
\end{equation}
The time-dependent coefficient reflects non-Markovian memory encoded in the RKHS---not a spatial fractional operator.

The operator derivative $D_X F \in L^2(\Omega; \Hi)$ is defined via Riesz representation:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:riesz-def}
\E[F \cdot \delta_X(u)] = \E[\ip{D_X F}{u}_\Hi] \quad \text{for all } u \in \Hi.
\end{equation}

