Let $Y = (Y_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$ be such that $Y_t\in\Dom(D)$ for a.e.\ $t$ and $t\mapsto \Pi DY_t$ lies in $L^2([0,T]\times\Omega;\HH)$. Define the \emph{intrinsic bracket}
\begin{equation}\label{eq:bracket}
\langle Y\rangle^{(D,\Pi)}_t := \int_0^t \norm{\Pi DY_s}_\HH^2\,ds.
\end{equation}

