B_t^\theta &:= -\int_0^t K(t,s)\,\theta_s\,d\bracket{M}_s. \label{eq:Btheta-def}
\end{align}
Under $\QQ$, the noise part $Z^{\QQ}$ is the same operator applied to a
martingale; the measure change induces the deterministic operator-valued
drift $B^\theta$.

