\label{rem:volterra}
For a Volterra process $X_t = \int_0^t K(t,s)\, dW_s$, one can define an energy space and stochastic integral (see, e.g., \cite{Nualart2006}), and the adjoint $D_X := \delta_X^*$ is well defined whenever $\delta_X$ is continuous. However, Volterra processes are generally not martingales (since $K(t,s)$ depends on~$t$), so the hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:CO}---particularly the representation property for~$X$ itself---are not directly satisfied.

