following_proof:
On the small-field region $\Omega_s=\{U:\theta_p<\theta_*\;\forall p\}$,
the local curvature bound gives a Poincar\'e constant
$\kappa_{\mathrm{loc}}=\frac{1}{2}+\beta\,\kappa_{\mathrm{eff}}(\theta_*)$
(Corollary~\ref{cor:curvature}).  By the Bakry--\'Emery
theorem~\cite{BakryEmery}, the conditional measure $\mu_s=\mu(\cdot\,|\,\Omega_s)$
satisfies $\mathrm{Var}_{\mu_s}(f)\le\kappa_{\mathrm{loc}}^{-1}
\mathcal{E}_{\mu_s}(f,f)$.

The Holley--Stroock perturbation lemma~\cite{HolleyStroock} relates the
spectral gap of $\mu$ to that of $\mu_s$.  Write
$d\mu/d\mu_s=\mu(\Omega_s)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\Omega_s}
+\mu(\Omega_s)\cdot(d\mu/d\mu_s-\mathbf{1}_{\Omega_s})$,
so the Radon--Nikodym ratio $d\mu/d\mu_s$ lies in
$[0,\,\mu(\Omega_s)^{-1}]$.  More precisely, for any test function $f$:
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Var}_\mu(f)\le\frac{1}{\mu(\Omega_s)^2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{\mu_s}(f)
+\mathrm{Var}_\mu(f\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\Omega_l}).
\end{equation}
The first term contributes $\kappa_{\mathrm{loc}}^{-1}/\mu(\Omega_s)^2$
to the Poincar\'e constant.  The second is controlled by
$\mu(\Omega_l)\le|\Lambda|\cdot e^{-c\beta}$ (chessboard estimate,
Theorem~\ref{thm:chess}).  Since
$-\log\mu(\Omega_s)=-\log(1-\mu(\Omega_l))\le 2\mu(\Omega_l)$
for $\mu(\Omega_l)<1/2$:
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{gap}(\mathcal{L})\ge\kappa_{\mathrm{loc}}
-2|\Lambda|e^{-c\beta}
=\tfrac{1}{2}+\beta\,\kappa_{\mathrm{eff}}(\theta_*)
-C'|\Lambda|e^{-c\beta}.
\end{equation}

