\label{thm:massgap}
At the matching scale $\beta_*$, the cluster expansion
(Theorem~\ref{thm:cluster}) provides exponential decay of
connected correlators of gauge-invariant observables with
decay rate $\kappa>0$ in block-lattice units:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:cluster-decay}
|\langle\mathcal{O}_1\mathcal{O}_2\rangle_c|
\le C\,\|\mathcal{O}_1\|\,\|\mathcal{O}_2\|\,
e^{-\kappa\,d(R_1,R_2)},
\end{equation}
uniformly in the volume $|\Lambda|$.  The mass gap at the
matching scale satisfies
\begin{equation}\label{eq:mgap}
m(\beta_*)\;\ge\;\frac{\kappa}{\ell_*}\;>\;0,
\end{equation}
where $\ell_*=2^{k_*}\cdot a$ is the block-lattice spacing
and $\kappa\ge\alpha=1$ from the KP weight function.

In the continuum limit:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:mgap-phys}
