\label{ass:exp-moment}
The stochastic-volatility model satisfies the exponential integrability
needed for the scenario-map estimates.  Concretely, for the values of
$r$ used in the hedging proof,
\begin{equation}
  \label{eq:exp-integrability-kernel}
  \E\bigl[\exp(r|V_t|)\bigr]<\infty,
  \qquad
  \sup_{t\le T}\E[\sigma_t^{4p}]<\infty .
\end{equation}
A sufficient condition for tempered stable drivers is the cumulant
condition
\begin{equation}
  \label{eq:cumulant-condition}
  \int_0^t\int_{\R}
  \left(e^{r|K(t,s)z|}-1-r|K(t,s)z|\mathbf 1_{|z|\le1}\right)
  \nu(dz)ds<\infty .
\end{equation}
For kernels bounded on the diagonal and tempered tails
$e^{-\lambda |z|}$, this holds for $r\|K\|_\infty<\lambda$.
For unregularized fractional kernels with $H<1/2$, this sufficient
condition generally fails because $K(t,s)$ is unbounded as $s\uparrow t$.

