  + \langle s_p^{(3)} \rangle_{\text{Gauss}}
  + \tfrac{1}{2}\langle (s_p^{(3)})^2 \rangle_{\text{Gauss}}^{\text{conn}}
  + \cdots
\end{equation}
where the Gaussian expectation is with respect to the
interior fields with the quadratic action $\bar{S}_B^{(2)}$.

The term $\langle s_p^{(3)} \rangle_{\text{Gauss}} = 0$
(cubic Gaussian moment vanishes). The connected
correlator $\langle (s_p^{(3)})^2 \rangle^{\text{conn}}$
is the one-loop correction to the coupling constant.

