By the martingale variance decomposition:
\begin{equation}
\Var(f) = \Var(\E[f|\cF_0]) + \sum_{k=1}^M \E[\Var(\E[f|\cF_k] \mid \cF_{k-1})].
\end{equation}
Each conditional variance term is controlled by the block Poincar\'e
inequality, which follows from the block curvature bound
(Corollary~\ref{cor:block-curv}) via the Bakry--\'Emery
implication~\eqref{eq:BE-implication}:
\begin{equation}
\Var(\E[f|\cF_k] \mid \cF_{k-1})
\leq \frac{1}{\kappa_B\beta}\,\E[|\nabla_{B_k} f|^2 \mid \cF_{k-1}].
\end{equation}
Summing over blocks and using the partition of unity
$\sum_k |\nabla_{B_k} f|^2 + |\nabla^{\mathrm{bdy}} f|^2
= |\nabla f|^2$ gives
\begin{equation}
\Var(f) \leq \frac{1}{\kappa_B\beta}\,\cE(f,f).
\end{equation}

