Assume \ref{assump:clustering}. Fix $j$ and choose $Z_j(a)$ by two-point normalization as in \eqref{eq:Zby2pt} (which forces nontriviality).
Then for each $n\ge 1$ and each $(\varphi_1,\dots,\varphi_n)$, the family $\{S_{n,a}^{(j)}(\varphi_1,\dots,\varphi_n)\}_{a>0}$ is bounded.
In particular, along any sequence $a_k\downarrow 0$, there exists a subsequence (still denoted $a_k$) such that
